# Changelog
All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]

### Changed (BREAKING)
- Migrated to Jackson 3: `jackson-databind`/`jackson-core` now use `tools.jackson.core` 3.1.8 and `@JsonNaming` is imported from `tools.jackson.databind.annotation` (`jackson-annotations` stays on `com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation`). Removed the `jackson.version.core` property.
- Added `Jackson3SerializationTest` (Role JSON round-trip with `tools.jackson`) and a JaCoCo method-coverage rule (minimum 85%).
- Added `docs/user-guide.md` and `docs/technical-guide.md` (Markdown, Mermaid diagrams) describing the migration.

### Fixed
- Aligned `jackson.annotations.version` in `bom/pom.xml` (2.20) with the root `pom.xml` (2.22).
- Removed the unused `org.webjars:webjars-locator-core` dependency (and its `webjars.locator.version` property) from `pom.xml` and `bom/pom.xml`; it was the only source of a Jackson 2 `jackson-core` (2.17.1) on the classpath. Only `jackson-annotations` remains under `com.fasterxml.jackson`, as required by Jackson 3.

### Security
- **`ci_settings.xml` no longer carries the Repsy credentials in clear text.** The account login was versioned in this public
  repository; it now reads `${env.REPSY_ACCOUNT_USER}` and `${env.REPSY_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD}`, like `persistence`. Removing it from
  the file does not remove it from the git history, so the Repsy password has to be rotated. `CiSettingsHygieneTest` fails the
  build if a literal credential comes back.

### Added (0.0.4-SNAPSHOT)
- `Contact.ownerType` / `Contact.ownerId` (getters, setters, `toString()`, `@JsonPropertyOrder`) for contacts of an
  external owner (e.g. a merchant of an application) that is neither a person nor an application.

### Added
- `Feature.roleIds` (`List<UUID>`) with getter/setter, included in `toString()`; used on creation to link a feature to existing roles.
- `LICENSE` file.
- README: centered header, grouped technology badges linking to each project, and a tech stack table covering all `pom.xml` versions (including Jackson Core and the Maven Compiler, PMD and Surefire plugins).

### Changed (BREAKING)
- Maven coordinates changed from `com.prx:prx-commons` to `com.umdc:commons`; Java packages moved from `com.prx.commons` to `com.umdc.commons`.
- `User.email` renamed to `User.emailAccount` (`getEmailAccount`/`setEmailAccount`).
- Project version bumped from `0.0.1` to `0.0.3`.
- Dependency upgrades: JUnit Jupiter 6.0.3 -> 6.1.3, Jackson annotations 2.20 -> 2.22, Jackson databind 2.21.4 -> 2.22.3, Gson 2.13.2 -> 2.14.0, org.json 20260522 -> 20260814, Log4j Core 2.25.4 -> 2.26.1.
- `jackson-core` is now managed in `dependencyManagement` (added `jackson.version.core` property).
- `AuditEventType` Javadoc rewritten: every constant is documented and the enum is described as mapping to the `general.audit_event.event_type` CHECK constraint.
- README: dependency badges, requirements, known issues, CI example and tech stack table updated to the `pom.xml` versions (Java 25, JUnit 6.1.3, Jackson 2.22.x, Gson 2.14.0, Log4j 2.26.1, org.json 20260814, Jakarta Validation 3.1.1); layout aligned with the mercury and backbone-rest READMEs; license section now points to `LICENSE`.
- `.gitignore` now ignores `commons.iml` and `dependencies_tree.txt`.

### Security
- Tests (`UserTest`, `MessengerTest`) no longer use hardcoded passwords; they use the `test.user.password` system property or a random UUID.

### Previously unreleased
- Documentation: translated build and README docs to English and updated them to reflect centralized versions (see `README.md`, `README-BUILD.md`, and `BUILD_VALIDATION_REPORT.md`).
- BOM and version management: dependency and plugin versions are centralized in the root `pom.xml` and a BOM is available at `bom/pom.xml` (artifact `com.prx:prx-commons-bom:0.0.1`).
- Build: default Java version set to 21 in the root `pom.xml`.
- Tests: prepared to add or update unit tests and test annotations (e.g., add `@DisplayName`) to meet coverage requirements.

## Version 0.0.1
- Updated dependencies.
- Added a class for secure SSL/HTTPS channel communication.
- Added `StandardException` class for capturing and propagating failures.
- Included authentication features.
